-## Parameter contract
+## Episode-fixed rule
 
-| Item | Contract |
+`selection_rule` has exactly three values, held fixed over every pair:
+
+| Value | Transformation |
 |---|---|
-| Parameter | `selection_metric`, exactly `"occupied_cells"` or `"bbox_area"` |
-| Original/default | `"occupied_cells"`; materialized source is byte-for-byte canonical |
-| Alternative | `"bbox_area"`; rank eligible objects by bounding-box area |
-| Episode selection | One `random.Random(seed).choice(...)` draw before any pair |
-| Complete episode | Three labeled demonstrations and one masked query |
-| Inputs | Four fixed lawful scenes with two eligible objects and one asymmetric distractor |
-| Input dependence | Evidence scenes deliberately reverse occupied-size and bbox-area order |
+| `occupied_cells` (default) | Find same-color four-connected components with width > 1 and a left-right symmetric raw bounding box; crop the largest by occupied-cell count. |
+| `bbox_area` | Use the same eligibility test and crop the eligible component with largest bounding-box area. |
+| `occupied_anchor_partner` | Select the occupied-cell winner, bind its color, then crop the unique other connected component with that color. |
 
